# Gitignored files copied into every worktree Claude Code creates.
# .gitignore syntax; only paths that match AND are gitignored are copied.
#
# Deliberately empty. The gitignored things a worktree needs are build/
# (3.2 GB) and snapshot/ (1.7 GB), and copying either per session is absurd —
# so scripts/lib/paths.sh arranges them on first use instead, and differently
# for each:
#
#   build/     a copy-on-write clone (0.38 s and 2.2 MB for 3.2 GB on APFS).
#              Cloned rather than linked so the worktree can run the pipeline
#              on top of it without rewriting another checkout's artifacts,
#              which every phase would otherwise do in place.
#   snapshot/  per-entry symlinks. Nothing rewrites a file in there and a
#              private copy would re-crawl upstream, so sharing is the goal.
#
# web/node_modules is cloned copy-on-write on first use by the same file.
# docs/ci.md §2, "Running in a git worktree", is the account of record.
#
# Add a line here if this project ever grows a small local file a worktree
# genuinely needs, such as a .env.
